# A Windows checkout gives a shell script CRLF endings, and a POSIX shell reads
# the carriage return as part of the last word on the line: `set -eu` becomes
# `set: Illegal option -`. The NT job runs these scripts inside WSL, so they
# must arrive with LF whatever the host does.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.dats text eol=lf
# A golden file is compared byte for byte, and a CRLF checkout fails every snapshot.
*.golden -text
